      "check": "balance",
      "difference": -44650,
      "source_page": 1,
      "note": "Statement of Financial Position business-type net position prints 1,279,109 (unrestricted 193,871), but the proprietary statements (p5, p6) and the Statement of Activities (p2) print 1,323,759 (unrestricted 238,521); the p1 Total column prints 2,433,603 vs p2's 2,478,253. p1 balances only by a 44,650 in 'Total current liabilities' 114,650 that no line shows (the only current line is 70,000) - the 44,650 equals the transfer to Water/Sewer. Balance-sheet business-type liabilities/net position taken from p5."
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Cash-basis governmental funds, accrual-basis business-type (Water/Sewer enterprise fund), as FY2023. Governmental receipts/disbursements from the Total column of the governmental funds statement (p4); transfers Total column net (44,650) out (Water/Sewer shows 44,650 in). Fund balance 1,071,460 -> 1,154,494 (p4); beginning cash not printed; ending cash = checking accounts 737,802 and certificates of deposit 416,692 (p3). Business-type receipts/expenses from p6 (operating revenue 358,520; nonoperating American Rescue Plan Act 71,680, recorded as federal grants; no single receipts total printed, so 430,200 is computed); total expenses 421,482 printed on p2 (operating 393,020 + interest 28,462). Net position 1,270,391 + 430,200 - 421,482 + 44,650 = 1,323,759. Proprietary cash flow statement (p7-8) left out (proprietary null for this cash-basis report, as FY2023): operating 35,287, capital and related financing (78,381), noncapital financing 71,680, cash 238,862 -> 267,448. Balance sheet: Statement of Financial Position (p1) assets; governmental cash/CD and fund balance lines from the governmental funds balance sheet Total column (p3, total 1,154,494 = p1 governmental column); business-type liabilities and net position from the proprietary statement (p5) because p1's business-type column does not agree (see report_discrepancies). Detail: the only governmental supplementary schedule is the combined all-governmental-funds budget schedule (p9; it classifies spending differently, e.g. Cultural and recreational 167,844), so detail is one line per fund column of the governmental funds statement (p4), as FY2023; Water/Sewer detail from its own cash-basis budget schedule (p10, budget and actual), with American Rescue Plan Act under its other financing sources. Read pages 1-10 of 10"
}
